\ The hand-threaded baseline for Phase 4 slice 6b's dogfood. Its combinator
\ twin `examples/filter_while.sth` expresses the same walk over
\ `filter`/`while` from `lib/combinators.sth`; the golden pins both to the
\ same output. The filter loop spells out the write cursor `filter` threads
\ (a manual `times` loop with the same `&arr i &> @` reads and
\ `&!arr over &!> v !` writes), and the fixpoint loop is a hand-written
\ self-tail-recursive word instead of `while`.

import: "../lib/combinators.sth" c | times | ;

: scores ( -- [i64 5] )
  0 5 fill | s |
  &!s 0 >usize &!> 3 !
  &!s 1 >usize &!> 7 !
  &!s 2 >usize &!> 1 !
  &!s 3 >usize &!> 9 !
  &!s 4 >usize &!> 5 !
  s ;

: fixpoint ( i64 -- i64 )
  dup 5 lt ~[ 1 add fixpoint ] ~[ ] if ;

: main ( -- )
  scores | arr |
  0 5 ~[ | i | &arr i >usize &> @ dup 4 gt ~[
          | v | &!arr over >usize &!> v ! 1 add
        ] ~[ drop ] if ] times
  | wf | arr drop
  wf .
  0 fixpoint . ;
